+# Producer4 finite asynchronous fresh guards
+
+SOURCE preparation only. This package has no executed models, started helper,
+new containers, grants, ordinary role windows or client qualification. All14
+failed attempts remain NO_CONTRIBUTION; the backend cause remains UNKNOWN.
+Independent SOURCE/control DATA/concrete review and a separate Root release are
+required. This is isolated E02 tooling, with no production SDK or architecture
+change.
+
+Each Node owner has one exact owned persistent Python interpreter and one
+byte-identical original `Lease` object. Every CHECK invokes the unchanged
+`Lease.check()` afresh. Interpreter reuse never authorizes a later action.
+Helper self and original guard source are rehashed per request; fixed runtime
+and loader are hashed on startup under the existing readonly bundle/image
+trust boundary. The original parent guards remain. No helper restart, lease
+renewal, previous reset, coalesced tick, cached OK or periodic permit exists.
+
+`guard-client-core.mjs` serializes short synchronous continuations. The one
+in-flight request and all queued entries share a64-entry/16MiB bound. A reply
+binds exact instance/run/lease/sequence/label/context/request bytes and is consumed
+once. The5s decision starts at submission, including queue and initial startup.
+The original operation/lease bounds are checked after context validation and
+immediately before the effect, without an intervening async yield. The terminal
+epoch/fault is checked again after a synchronous effect, so an effect that
+cancels its owner cannot retain a success row. Timers and socket/helper/capture
+faults fence outside the queue. Cleanup cannot erase the first fault.
+
+Production UTC/BOOT observations are conservative intervals: Date.now has a1ms
+quantum; /proc/uptime exposes an explicit decimal quantum (usually10ms).
+MONOTONIC samples bracket this bounded proc read. Enqueue uses lower bounds,
+consume uses upper bounds, so adding5s to a rounded enqueue upper bound cannot
+extend the decision. UTC/BOOT/MONO enqueue deadlines all apply; a held response
+across suspend cannot survive by relying on a paused MONOTONIC timer. Exact
+original Python clock samples stay decimal strings in the raw reply. This is
+cooperative Linux timing under the original host/time-namespace assumptions,
+with conservative early refusal; it is not atomic multi-clock or crossprocess
+revocation attestation. This interval strategy still requires independent
+SOURCE assessment and actual suspend/clock adversary evidence before release.
+
+A protected effect is synchronous; a thenable effect is refused. Prepare,
+publish and native validation retain15 original internal guard positions in
+synchronous generators. Each protected generator.next executes within its fresh
+guard. A yielded network wait runs outside the executor; resumption performs
+only lexical assignment/loop predicate until the next guard yield. The existing
+Rust spawnSync remains independently bounded8s and is not called nonblocking.
+Its position and limit are unchanged. This package does not establish general
+event-loop responsiveness.
+
+Proxy APP callback receipt immediately increments a denial-only input epoch,
+before queueing or parsing. Backend continuations retain this epoch, actual
+buffer hash, subscription generation and publication attempt, then revalidate
+at send/completion. Socket close invalidates the connection epoch immediately.
+Old deliveries cannot become a later stage's receipt. These stricter refusal
+paths and all async aliases still need independent complete coverage review.
+
+Query10s, handshake3s, fixture command55s, controller45s, ordinary lease1800s,
+original guard15s gap, resources and original shared16MiB capture remain.
+The initial query/handshake budget includes constructor-queue wait rather than
+starting later; this can refuse sooner. Two seconds of each Node owner's
+existing55/1800 budget are reserved for child cleanup. No new cleanup duration
+is added. Cleanup signal dispatch rechecks remaining time and targets only the
+exact owned ChildProcess handle. Exhausted deadlines record negative unresolved
+host-owned cleanup; no late signal or fabricated reap is claimed. The parent
+owns its existing finite container/command cleanup. A stopped host cannot
+execute cleanup and these bounds make no stronger hard-realtime claim.
+
+The serve watchdog retains every original1s tick. A controller also performs a
+fresh1s watchdog CHECK while waiting for its control reply, so the persistent
+original Lease.previous cannot silently acquire a15s observation gap during an
+otherwise allowed45s control wait. These additional checks are not permits;
+every original effect still has its own fresh request.
+
+Orderly CLOSE requires zero pending checks and no future protected work. A
+normal controller CLOSE affects only that controller's child; the separate
+serve helper continues. Natural exit/stdout EOF/stderr EOF/close are observed
+as Node child events. They are not Python waitpid/Popen/reap proof. Other child
+failure/EOF/stderr is sticky negative, with live helper original revocation and
+original parent failure propagation. A dead helper is never said to have
+written REVOKED. Startup/import/controller failures cancel and attempt a
+bounded owned drain before main exits. Service signal CLOSE is allowed only
+with zero pending work; otherwise it is terminal negative.
+
+`guard-dto-contract.json` defines profilev3/commandv3/callv2/observerv3
+observations. Global phase sequence remains integer1..N; helper sequence is
+`guardSequence`. ENTRY/REQUEST/REPLY/consumed EXIT correlate by exact instance,
+sequence and bytes, not adjacency. Consumed EXIT includes the final direct
+clock bounds as decimal strings. External REVOKED metadata is checked again
+before consumption; future revocation after the last check is not atomic.
+
+The independently adopted accounting addendum fixes the original MEDIUM gap.
+The original16MiB is partitioned8MiB service plus64x128KiB parent-owned
+controller attempts. Service includes4KiB global host header/footer,4KiB Node
+RPC diagnostics and8MiB-minus8KiB for every Node-service put/phase/proxy proof.
+Its pure account exists before helper startup; startup immutable rows and later
+phase flush are conservatively both charged. Exactly one serve process owns
+the two streams. Controller watchdogs write only their own local staged audit.
+
+Every attempted Runtime.fixture call permanently debits its128KiB slot before
+inspect/launch/first proof, including failures. The host-only ledger is outside
+fixture-writable mounts. Each slot contains120KiB encoded proof,4KiB parent
+ledger/status and4KiB diagnostics. Before audit append, exact immutable UTF-8
+JSON/base64/comma encodings are charged;1024 bytes inside the proof share
+prepay its closed envelope/delimiters. One exact stdout emission consumes this
+credit; duplicate emission fails. The changed Android driver verifies and
+reuses the actual existing command.stdout Pin, avoiding a second retained RPC
+copy. Pre-write bounds supply admission; later sums are consistency only.
+
+No refund/retry/partial repair or independent1MiB RPC allowance exists. Partial
+durable writes poison before future effects and preserve the original fault.
+Node stdout.write's Boolean is not a byte count. Parent actual complete capture,
+EOF/natural lifecycle and whole current consumer joins remain mandatory. A
+parent failure is sticky through the existing Lease/owned cleanup path; no
+atomic global crossprocess poison is claimed. A service can process within its
+already reserved share until it observes that original failure; the whole role
+is unqualified. The partition may refuse a workload formerly using all16MiB
+for the service; no measured-fit guarantee follows.
+
+Terminal helper EOF/exit/close/owned-signal facts may be retained after the
+local protocol fence under an explicit allowlist and the same counter. No late
+protocol/send/GUARD_EXIT success can use that retention path. Drain is bounded
+and shared across concurrent failure handlers; stream closure follows the
+observed drain/failure, not a fabricated child lifecycle. Final observer state
+is labelled BEFORE_THIS_FINAL_RECORD_WRITE. Intended/admitted charged bytes
+are not physical-byte attestation. No old producer3 DATA or reviews transfer.
+
+`test_guard_client.mjs` contains memory-mocked scheduler/wire/proxy fence
+regressions, not real helper throughput. The separate fixed
+`probe-guard-helper.mjs` is an unexecuted actual-helper latency/timer recipe.
+It needs a separately reviewed exact no-network container/mount/input/lease/
+root release and cleanup envelope. It does not boot Android, query a relay or
+qualify a client. Warm helper performance and full negative owned-helper IO/
+clock/revocation/cleanup behavior remain actual DATA gates.
